ce's April 2015 Mutual Evaluation Report on Australia's progress in combatting money laundering and terrorist financing stated that Australia is an attractive destination for foreign proceeds of crime, particularly corruption-related proceeds flowing into real estate,* >> >> *(v) the December 2017 OECD Phase 4 Report on Australia's implementation of the OECD Anti-Bribery Convention recommended that Australia address the risk that the real estate sector could be used to launder the proceeds of foreign bribery,* >> >> *(vi) Australia is one of only six countries in the world not to have included real estate agents, accountants and","result":"negative","slug":"division-federal-senate-6133","source_url":"https://theyvoteforyou.org.au/divisions/senate/2019-12-04/10"}
